.\" Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-fable-5-2
.\" Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-sonnet-5-5
.Dd November 14, 2026
.Dt EMACS-RELEASE-PLAN 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm emacs-release-plan
.Nd plan to release the Emacs distribution 1.0 on 18 December 2026
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Bd -ragged -offset indent
Plan, not started.
EM6 has owner steps that deploy
.Ql docs.example.org
and redirect the old site; it changes a service and DNS.
No step changes a host.
EM6 carries its rollback and checks below.
.Ed
.Pp
The Emacs distribution is the third release of
.Xr jylhis-ship-plan 7 .
The owner uses it each day.
Its largest task is a standalone entry point, which the ledger did not list.
.Ss State on 2026-11-14
.Bl -bullet
.It
Verified: the checks
.Ql emacs-elisp-lint ,
.Ql emacs-module-eval ,
.Ql emacs-docs-ds-in-sync
and
.Ql emacs-docs-build
pass.
.It
Not verified:
.Ql emacs-elisp-test ,
.Ql emacs-elisp-compile
and
.Ql emacs-config-startup .
The cloud container could not download the package sources.
EM4 runs them on local-lab.
Since this page was written,
.Ql just test
runs the ERT suite natively (commit c6ea62497f), and the ERT check writes a
JUnit report (commit b7095b1d8c).
Neither change makes the three checks above verified.
.It
The distribution has no flake and no
.Ql package.nix .
It imports
.Ql nix/inputs.nix ,
.Ql nix/tamal/lock.json ,
.Ql platform/kit
and
.Ql projects/libs/design .
An outside user needs a checkout of the whole tree today.
.It
The licence is set: GPL-3.0-or-later in
.Ql project.nix ,
.Ql LICENSE
and the README; the file headers are not uniform.
.It
14 test files cover 35 Lisp files; 47 fragments wait; no version is set.
.It
emacs-overlay is in use, and Emacs 31.1 comes from the binary cache.
.It
.Ql docs.example.org
is not deployed, by TODO.md; the cloud container could not reach the address.
.El
.Ss Selected approach
.Bl -bullet
.It
One flake in the project directory serves the tree and the public repository,
so the two cannot differ.
.It
The design assets and the kit helpers that the distribution uses go into the
export through
.Ql publish.vendor ,
as marchyo does.
.It
The landing page is the existing front page of emacs-docs, with the support
section of the kit.
.El
.Ss Alternatives
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It A synthesized flake
The publish tool can write a flake for a project with a
.Ql package.nix .
The distribution has none and has many inputs, so a written flake is clearer.
.It twist.nix as the build layer
The ledger names it as one option.
emacs-overlay already does that job in the tree, with cache parity, so a
change gives nothing for 1.0.
.El
.Ss Definition of done
.Bl -bullet
.It
The public repository exists under the name of EM1.
.It
.Ql nix flake check
passes in a fresh clone, with no access to jylhis.
.It
.Ql nix run github:Jylhis/<name>
starts Emacs with the configuration.
.It
The installation page describes the Home Manager module and the NixOS module,
and a test evaluates each.
.It
The checks
.Ql emacs-elisp-test ,
.Ql emacs-elisp-compile
and
.Ql emacs-config-startup
pass, with the result on record.
.It
.Ql https://docs.example.org
answers with status 200; the old Pages addresses redirect to it.
.It
The tag
.Ql v1.0.0
exists in the public repository, with a release and its notes.
.It
Each Lisp file has the licence header.
.It
The landing page names the issue tracker, a mail address and the release feed.
.It
.Ql just release-verify emacs
exits with 0.
.El
.Ss Tasks
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It EM1 (owner; 15 minutes; after nothing)
Decide the public name and repository of the distribution.
The old public site used the name jotain.
Confirm or change the licence, which is GPL-3.0-or-later today.
.It EM2 (opus design, then sonnet; 4 sessions; after nothing)
Give the distribution a standalone entry point.
Add
.Ql flake.nix
with the inputs that
.Ql nix/inputs.nix
supplies today.
Replace each import of
.Ql platform/kit
and
.Ql projects/libs/design
with a flake input or a
.Ql publish.vendor
entry.
The monorepo build keeps one code path with the export.
.It EM3 (sonnet; 2 sessions; after EM2, RK4)
Add the
.Ql publish
block.
Make
.Ql just publish-verify
pass on the export:
.Ql nix flake check
without the monorepo.
.It EM4 (sonnet; 1 session; after nothing)
Run
.Ql emacs-elisp-test ,
.Ql emacs-elisp-compile
and
.Ql emacs-config-startup
on local-lab and record the results here.
The session of 2026-11-14 ran in a cloud container, where the package sources
returned HTTP 403.
.It EM5 (sonnet; 1 session; after EM2)
Rewrite
.Ql docs/installation.mdx
for the flake: try it with
.Ql nix run ,
install with the Home Manager module, install with the NixOS module.
Correct the platform statement so that it matches
.Ql project.nix .
.It EM6 (owner, then haiku; owner 30 minutes, 1 session; after nothing)
Owner: confirm the two Cloudflare Actions secrets, run the infra plan and
apply for
.Ql docs.example.org ,
and merge so that the workflow deploys.
Then redirect the old GitHub Pages site.
.Pp
Idempotent: the infra apply and the redirect are idempotent;
the merge is not, and a second merge is a new commit.
Rollback: before the redirect, remove the DNS record of the site and apply again;
after the redirect, revert the redirect commit of the old site.
This restores the old GitHub Pages site as the only address.
No step of EM6 deletes the old site, so this rollback stays possible.
Expected state: the plan shows one new Worker route and one DNS record;
the old address answers with a redirect.
Check: run
.Ql just infra-plan cloudflare
before the apply and read it;
then run
.Ql curl -sI https://docs.example.org
and expect a status 200, and run
.Ql curl -sI
on the old address and expect a status 301.
No command of this step ran for this plan; all are unverified.
.Pp
Known effects:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
DNS takes minutes to propagate; the site can answer 404 or a certificate error in that time.
.It
Visitors of the old address land on the new landing page; old deep links can fail.
.It
Each push to green main starts a Workers Builds run (free tier).
.El
.It EM7 (sonnet; 1 session; after EM6, RK2)
Add the
.Ql Support and updates
section, the version and the install command to the landing page of
.Ql projects/services/emacs-docs .
.It EM8 (haiku; 1 session; after EM1)
Give each file under
.Ql lisp/
the same licence header.
Add a
.Ql LICENSE
file and
.Ql meta.license
to emacs-docs.
.It EM9 (sonnet; 1 session; after EM3)
Add a workflow to the export that builds the distribution from the public
repository and starts it in batch mode.
.It EM10 (sonnet, then owner; 1 session, owner 15 minutes; after EM3 to EM9, RK5, RK9)
Set
.Ql meta.version ,
cut 1.0.0 from the 47 fragments.
Owner: create the repository, publish and push the tag.
Run
.Ql just release-verify emacs
and record the output.
.El
.Ss Schedule
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It W4, 7 to 13 December
EM1 to EM6, EM8; the site is deployed.
.It W5, 14 to 20 December
EM7, EM9, EM10; the release is on Friday 18 December.
.El
.Ss Goals
.Bl -bullet
.It
4 December: no task is due; the work starts on 7 December.
.It
11 December: 7 of 10 tasks; the flake evaluates in the tree;
.Ql docs.example.org
answers and the export passes its check.
.It
18 December: 10 of 10 tasks; every line of the definition of done is true.
.El
.Ss After 1.0
.Bl -bullet
.It
1.1: the review queue for merge requests and pull requests with a viewed
state.
.It
1.2: the daily code excerpt on the dashboard.
.It
Later: dokja as an xref backend, after the dokja cut-over.
.It
Later: context as a value and capability rings for the AI commands.
.It
Not a condition: the igc trial stays an owner item.
.El
